cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EcoFate or build on it, please cite it as below."
title: "EcoFate: screening-level chemical exposure and risk assessments"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Hernandez-Betancur"
    given-names: "Jose"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2652-1405"
abstract: >-
  EcoFate turns fragmented environmental data into screening-level chemical exposure risk
  profiles. It unifies public datasets, such as the EPA Toxics Release Inventory (TRI), with
  phenomenological transport models to automate screening-level exposure assessments. A user
  provides a location, facility, or chemical of interest, and the system pulls together release
  data, chemical properties, and transport modeling to return a risk profile: a starting point
  for further investigation.
# Concept DOI: resolves to the latest archived release (each release also has its own DOI).
